warning[bool_to_int_with_if]: a `bool` is turned into an integer with a branch
  --> tests/lint/bool_to_int_with_if/bad.jai:12:10
   |
12 |     a := ifx ready then 1 else 0;
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(s64) ready`
   |
12 ~     a := cast(s64) ready;
   |

warning[bool_to_int_with_if]: a `bool` is turned into an integer with a branch
  --> tests/lint/bool_to_int_with_if/bad.jai:13:10
   |
13 |     b := ifx count > 3 then 0 else 1;
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(s64) (count <= 3)`
   |
13 ~     b := cast(s64) (count <= 3);
   |

warning[bool_to_int_with_if]: a `bool` is turned into an integer with a branch
  --> tests/lint/bool_to_int_with_if/bad.jai:14:17
   |
14 |     small: u8 = ifx ready then 1 else 0;
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(u8) ready`
   |
14 ~     small: u8 = cast(u8) ready;
   |

warning[bool_to_int_with_if]: a `bool` is turned into an integer with a branch
  --> tests/lint/bool_to_int_with_if/bad.jai:16:5
   |
16 |     if ready n = 1;
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(s64) ready`
   |
16 -     if ready n = 1;
17 -     else n = 0;
16 +     n = cast(s64) ready;
   |

warning[bool_to_int_with_if]: a `bool` is turned into an integer with a branch
  --> tests/lint/bool_to_int_with_if/bad.jai:19:5
   |
19 |     if count > 2 {
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: write `cast(s64) (count <= 2)`
   |
19 -     if count > 2 {
20 -         c.hits = 0;
21 -     } else {
22 -         c.hits = 1;
23 -     }
19 +     c.hits = cast(s64) (count <= 2);
   |
